# 18. FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The remediation is considered complete only when the product:

1. Looks like one coherent professional product.
2. Has a mobile navbar that works without clipping or overlap.
3. Has a clear, deliberate color hierarchy.
4. Uses consistent typography and spacing.
5. Has consistent controls and interactive states.
6. Works at all required viewport widths.
7. Meets the existing UI UX Pro Max workflow requirements.
8. Does not contain superficial CSS hacks that conceal root causes.
9. Passes build, type-check, and lint validation.
10. Is reviewed as a production-quality frontend, not merely a working prototype.

